6. Full Mathematical Conjecture Specification
6.1 Mathematical Conjecture Schema
The mathematical conjecture schema defines the structure of a mathematical conjecture deposit.

It has the following fields:

conjecture_id. A string. Required.

conjecture_name. A string. Required.

statement_formal. A string. Required.

statement_informal. A string. Required.

field. A string. Required.

subfield. A string. Optional.

status. An enum. Required. The values are open, proved, disproved, partially_resolved, undecided.

history. An object. Required. It contains author, year, and publication_reference.

prize. An object. Optional. It contains prize_name, prize_amount, and prize_conditions.

partial_results. An array of partial_result objects. Optional.

implications. An array of implication objects. Optional.

counterexamples. An array of counterexample objects. Optional.

computational_checks. An array of check objects. Optional.

known_bounds. An array of bound objects. Optional.

related_conjectures. An array of conjecture relations. Optional.

proof_reference. A string. Optional.

disproof_reference. A string. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

verification_result_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

The history object has:

author. An array of strings.

year. An integer.

publication_reference. A string.

The prize object has:

prize_name. A string.

prize_amount. An object. Optional. It contains value and currency.

prize_conditions. A string.

Each partial_result object has:

result_id. A string.

result_description. A string.

result_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

prover. An array of strings.

reference. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each implication object has:

implication_id. A string.

implication_description. A string.

implication_direction. An enum. The values are follows_from_conjecture, follows_from_negation, bidirectional.

implication_target. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each counterexample object has:

counterexample_id. A string.

counterexample_description. A string.

counterexample_status. An enum. The values are confirmed, suspected, refuted, unclear.

reference. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each check object has:

check_id. A string.

check_description. A string.

check_bound. An object. It contains value and units.

check_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

checker. A string.

reference. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each bound object has:

bound_id. A string.

bound_description. A string.

bound_value. An object. It contains value and units.

bound_direction. An enum. The values are upper_bound, lower_bound, exact.

reference. A string.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each conjecture relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_conjecture_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are implies, implied_by, equivalent, generalizes, special_case, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

