7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Mathematical Conjecture
function createMathematicalConjecture(conjecture, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the conjecture against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the verification result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. Generate a conjecture ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 6. Insert the mathematical conjecture.

Step 7. Insert the partial results, the implications, the counterexamples, the computational checks, the bounds, and the conjecture relations.

Step 8. Insert the work link and the verification link if present.

Step 9. Insert the provenance.

Step 10. Insert the moderation record.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the conjecture_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Mathematical Conjecture
function readMathematicalConjecture(conjectureId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the conjecture. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the partial results, the implications, the counterexamples, the computational checks, the bounds, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Mathematical Conjecture
function updateMathematicalConjecture(conjectureId, conjecture, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing conjecture. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new conjecture.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the conjecture_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Mathematical Conjecture
function deleteMathematicalConjecture(conjectureId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing conjecture. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the conjecture_id and the status deleted.

