12. Validation Engine Design
The registry validates the following.

Validation 1. Conjecture validity. Every conjecture is validated against the schema.

Validation 2. Referential integrity.

Validation 3. Version chain acyclicity.

Validation 4. Work resolution.

Validation 5. Verification result resolution.

Validation 6. Provenance completeness.

Validation 7. Audit completeness.

Validation 8. Moderation completeness.

Validation 9. Status consistency. The status must be consistent with the proof and disproof references.

Validation 10. Implication consistency. The implication target must resolve to a conjecture or be flagged.

Validation 11. Bound consistency. The bounds must be consistent with the computational checks.

Validation 12. Counterexample consistency. The counterexample status must be consistent with the conjecture status.

